.TH "tum\-flip" "1" "" "" "tmux\-borrow Manual"
.SS NAME
\f[B]tum\-flip\f[R] \[em] hide or show a borrowed thing by slot, or
context\-aware
.SS SYNOPSIS
\f[B]tum flip\f[R] [\f[I]slot\f[R]]
.PP
\f[B]tum flip\f[R] \f[B]\-h\f[R] | \f[B]\[en]help\f[R]
.SS DESCRIPTION
Toggle a borrowed thing between shown and hidden.
With a \f[I]slot\f[R] (a single character in \f[CR]0\[en]9\f[R] or
\f[CR]a\[en]z\f[R]), toggle the thing bound to that slot in the current
host window.
Hide parks the pane in the hidden session (clears \f[CR]host\f[R],
captures geometry); show brings it back beside its host and restores the
recorded geometry.
.PP
With no slot, \f[B]tum flip\f[R] is context\-aware: from a focused
borrowed pane it toggles just that pane; from a host with one borrowed
thing it toggles that; from a host with several it opens the chooser.
An owned utility flipped back from hidden returns only to its home pane;
a flip from another pane does nothing to it.
.PP
A layout\[cq]s slot toggles \f[B]all\f[R] its members as a group: a
group hide hides every member (including any individually shown); a
group show shows every member (including any individually hidden).
A member\[cq]s own slot toggles just that member, which a later group
show brings back.
The process is never restarted \[em] only moved.
.SS OPTIONS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\[en]help\f[R] Print a short synopsis (the SYNOPSIS
and EXAMPLES sections of this page) and exit.
For bare \f[B]tum\f[R], list every subcommand.
.SS EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
tum flip 1               # hide or show the thing in slot 1
tum flip                 # context\-aware: focused pane, or host\[aq]s single, or chooser
tum flip d               # toggle the whole \[aq]dev\[aq] layout group
.EE
